<title>GREECE: Cut-off price at 10-yr Greek bond auction at 98.61.</title>
<headline>Cut-off price at 10-yr Greek bond auction at 98.61.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following information on the auction of Greek three-, five-, seven- and 10-year fixed coupon bonds was provided by the Bank of Greece.</p>
<p>   Term				     10-years</p>
<p>   Coupon				    8.80%</p>
<p>   Face value			     1.0 million drachmas</p>
<p>   Min price accepted		   986,100</p>
<p>   Aver price accepted		  991,971</p>
<p>   Max offered price		   1,006,897.78</p>
<p>   Competitive amount		   100 bln drachmas</p>
<p>   Settlement date			June 19, 97</p>
<p>   Issue date			 March 21, 1997</p>
<p>   Term			    3-yr	 5-yr	   7-yr</p>
<p>   Auction date		     June 17, 1997</p>
<p>   Coupon			  9.8%	 9.2%	   8.9%</p>
<p>   Face value			    1.0 million drachmas</p>
<p>   Min price accepted    1,001,000     992,500	987,700</p>
<p>   Aver price accepted   1,004,658     998,133	994,752</p>
<p>   Max price accepted    1,019,260    1,013,800    1,010,231</p>
<p>   Competitive amount     50 bln drs  50bln drs   50bln drs</p>
<p>   Non-competitive amount   N/A	   N/A	   N/A</p>
<p>   Settlement			  June 19, 1997</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
